{"id":"scripts/bulk-upload.mjs","pkg":"scripts","kind":"script","lines":216,"commentLines":51,"header":["I use this to bulk-upload circulars through the REAL POST /api/circulars endpoint, the exact same backend path the admin modal uses (OCR -> chunk -> embed -> atomic DB transaction -> blob store). No shortcuts, no direct DB writes. It is driven entirely by a manifest CSV, so the title<->file pairing is the one I verified, never guessed at upload time. PREREQUISITES:","1. Dev server running: npm run dev","2. Manifest CSV present (below): circulars_manifest.csv","3. The 50 PDFs on disk under a root you pass with --files","MANIFEST COLUMNS (header row required): filename,folder,confirmed_title,publishedAt_YYYY-MM-DD,status,evidence_notes","- filename : e.g. 07_2023.pdf","- folder : the sub-folder under --files that holds the PDF","- confirmed_title : the headline to store (exact wording)","- publishedAt_YYYY-MM-DD : issue date, strict YYYY-MM-DD (status / evidence_notes are ignored by this script, they are for you.)","USAGE: node scripts/bulk-upload.mjs \\ --manifest ./circulars_manifest.csv \\ --files \"/path/to/2026 to 2022\" \\ --ticket 400000 Flags: --manifest <path> CSV path (default ./circulars_manifest.csv) --files <dir> root dir that contains the year sub-folders --ticket <no> authorTicketNo to stamp (must start with 4 to allow later edit/delete by that executive). Optional. --base <url> default http://localhost:3000 --yes skip the interactive confirm (for CI); default asks --start <n> 1-based row to start from (resume after a failure) BEHAVIOUR:","- It prints the full pairing table, then WAITS for you to type \"yes\".","- It uploads strictly in manifest order, one at a time (serials are assigned per-year by the backend; sequential upload keeps them deterministic).","- It HALTS on the first failure and tells you which row, so that a bad upload can never silently corrupt the set. Re-run with --start <n> to resume."],"symbols":[{"name":"arg","kind":"function","exported":false,"isDefault":false,"async":false,"line":50,"sig":"function arg(name, def = undefined)","params":[{"name":"name","type":"","optional":false,"rest":false,"def":""},{"name":"def","type":"","optional":true,"rest":false,"def":"undefined"}],"returns":"","generics":"","doc":["---------- tiny arg parser ----------"],"paramDocs":{},"returnDoc":"","id":"719e1ac344-arg","usedBy":[]},{"name":"MANIFEST","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":57,"sig":"const MANIFEST = arg(\"manifest\", \"./circulars_manifest.csv\")","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"719e1ac344-MANIFEST","usedBy":[]},{"name":"FILES_ROOT","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":58,"sig":"const FILES_ROOT = arg(\"files\", \".\")","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"719e1ac344-FILES_ROOT","usedBy":[]},{"name":"TICKET","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":59,"sig":"const TICKET = arg(\"ticket\", \"\")","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"719e1ac344-TICKET","usedBy":[]},{"name":"BASE","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":60,"sig":"const BASE = arg(\"base\", \"http://localhost:3000\")","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"719e1ac344-BASE","usedBy":[]},{"name":"SKIP_CONFIRM","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":61,"sig":"const SKIP_CONFIRM = !!arg(\"yes\", false)","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"719e1ac344-SKIP_CONFIRM","usedBy":[]},{"name":"START","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":62,"sig":"const START = parseInt(arg(\"start\", \"1\"), 10) || 1","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"719e1ac344-START","usedBy":[]},{"name":"parseCSV","kind":"function","exported":false,"isDefault":false,"async":false,"line":65,"sig":"function parseCSV(text)","params":[{"name":"text","type":"","optional":false,"rest":false,"def":""}],"returns":"","generics":"","doc":["---------- minimal CSV parser (handles quoted fields + commas) ----------"],"paramDocs":{},"returnDoc":"","id":"719e1ac344-parseCSV","usedBy":[]},{"name":"raw